WEBVTT

02:41.260 --> 02:43.230
Nothing's changed.

02:43.490 --> 02:45.660
It's just like it was three years ago.

03:16.990 --> 03:21.060
Iason-sama, you had no departure leave yesterday.

03:21.060 --> 03:23.030
Are you sure it's okay?

03:23.070 --> 03:25.070
What's wrong, Katze?

03:25.640 --> 03:32.010
Nothing, it's just that Kasala seems to be taking diplomacy issues much more seriously after that previous incident.

03:32.710 --> 03:38.250
I prepared a private shuttle for you yesterday, thinking you may be in a hurry.

03:40.520 --> 03:42.090
Don't worry.

03:42.520 --> 03:48.160
It's nice to take a long trip in a civilian spaceship once in a while.

03:48.560 --> 03:52.700
To top that, I've managed to secure the VIP using my special status.

03:53.060 --> 03:56.800
I feel there is a problem in security too.

03:56.830 --> 04:00.770
The security guards at the front door are more than enough.

04:00.800 --> 04:03.040
There's no need for excess.

04:04.510 --> 04:09.580
It's not like there's anyone waiting for me to get home.

04:12.480 --> 04:16.490
Seems like the rumors were true. Iason did release Riki.

04:17.590 --> 04:21.190
There's no sign that Riki was disposed of in Midas.

04:21.220 --> 04:25.500
In that case, maybe he was disposed of by the government.

04:26.900 --> 04:29.830
It's about the Elemina Jump Gate, isn't it.

04:34.210 --> 04:34.990
Yes.

04:35.610 --> 04:40.580
If it all goes well, we can return to Amoi on the afternoon of the 2nd.

05:01.960 --> 05:04.570
Midas, the city that never sleeps.

05:05.330 --> 05:08.440
For those who have too much money and time,

05:08.470 --> 05:14.580
this is an ideal Shangri-La for the fulfillment of all desires.

05:28.520 --> 05:29.330
Move!

05:42.470 --> 05:43.470
Shit...!

05:49.650 --> 05:51.810
Mongrels of the Slum.

05:51.850 --> 05:54.380
Seems like they've stepped onto the wrong turf.

06:13.900 --> 06:19.880
Ceres is a ghost area wiped out of Midas.

06:22.600 --> 06:26.620
For Slum residents without a Midas ID,

06:26.620 --> 06:29.220
it's natural that they have no human rights.

08:36.310 --> 08:37.750
Shit...!

08:37.810 --> 08:39.820
Jeeks! They won't give up!

09:02.270 --> 09:03.870
Die!

09:10.210 --> 09:11.810
Score!

09:11.850 --> 09:15.820
Shit! How could I get half-killed in a place like this?!

09:41.610 --> 09:43.850
Where the hell is this?

09:58.530 --> 09:59.600
Who's that?

10:05.470 --> 10:06.770
Is he there?

10:06.800 --> 10:08.800
No.

10:09.110 --> 10:12.780
I told you, you should've finished him off instead of fooling around.

10:13.380 --> 10:16.380
But he runs fast!

10:16.450 --> 10:17.650
What're we gonna do?

10:17.680 --> 10:19.480
He saw my face.

10:19.520 --> 10:21.120
So what?

10:21.120 --> 10:24.050
You just need to finish him off cleanly.

10:24.090 --> 10:27.190
He's gotta be the weakest!

10:27.220 --> 10:29.290
Those brats!

10:35.660 --> 10:37.070
Hey, you.

10:37.100 --> 10:39.240
What're you doing there?

10:44.170 --> 10:47.940
You brats should go home, take a piss, and get to bed.

10:47.980 --> 10:50.910
Huh? Where did that moron come from?

10:50.950 --> 10:56.450
Oh? Bro, you do know who you're speaking to, don't you?

10:56.590 --> 10:58.450
We're Jeeks!

11:02.860 --> 11:08.230
Jeeks? No idea. Sounds like crap.

11:08.230 --> 11:10.630
You have no idea who us Jeeks are?!

11:10.670 --> 11:12.540
Are you an idiot?

11:12.540 --> 11:15.670
If he doesn't know, let's teach him.

11:16.510 --> 11:19.780
The Slum will always be Slum.

11:19.810 --> 11:22.610
You're a huge step down from the kids in Eos.

11:23.510 --> 11:26.220
Come down, bro.

11:26.250 --> 11:29.190
I'll slice off that mouth of yours!

12:00.120 --> 12:01.580
An eye for an eye.

12:01.580 --> 12:03.620
And throw in some meat and bone.

12:03.650 --> 12:07.260
This is the way of the Slum.

12:38.120 --> 12:39.690
Wow...

12:46.660 --> 12:49.370
Seriously, that was annoying.

13:01.910 --> 13:04.350
Overkill much?

13:04.380 --> 13:08.380
Look, the Jeeks are just a bunch of brats.

13:08.880 --> 13:11.150
Hey, Kirie. You okay?

13:11.190 --> 13:13.060
Answer if you're alive!

13:13.090 --> 13:15.720
Geez, what took you so long?.!

13:15.790 --> 13:18.090
Did you do all this?

13:18.130 --> 13:19.430
No way.

13:19.500 --> 13:23.030
Of course, if you were this strong,

13:23.070 --> 13:26.400
you wouldn't need to rely on us.

13:28.440 --> 13:29.710
Shut the hell up!

13:29.770 --> 13:31.510
Who was it, then?

13:31.540 --> 13:32.910
Like hell I'd know!

13:34.780 --> 13:36.750
You haven't changed a bit.

13:41.220 --> 13:42.650
It can't be...

13:52.860 --> 13:54.160
Riki?

13:55.730 --> 13:57.900
Yo, Guy.

13:57.930 --> 13:59.840
It's been three years.

13:59.870 --> 14:02.670
Are you really... Riki?

14:02.710 --> 14:04.240
No way... For real?

14:04.270 --> 14:05.670
I don't believe it!

14:39.610 --> 14:40.540
Riki...

14:40.880 --> 14:41.910
Riki, really?

14:42.510 --> 14:46.020
He's Riki, the former head of Bison?

15:11.840 --> 15:13.280
Hey, did you hear?

15:13.310 --> 15:14.310
Hear what?

15:14.340 --> 15:15.880
It's Riki.

15:15.910 --> 15:19.080
Oh yeah, I heard. He's back, right?

15:19.110 --> 15:20.520
Huh? No way!

15:20.550 --> 15:23.750
Wasn't he working as a delivery guy under Zack?

15:23.750 --> 15:26.520
He's been set back three years.

15:27.360 --> 15:31.460
So he's just another Slum mongrel like us, after all.

15:43.840 --> 15:46.440
Hey hey, who's that "Riki"?

15:46.480 --> 15:49.350
Huh? You don't know?

15:49.380 --> 15:50.580
Nah.

15:50.610 --> 15:51.410
Really?

15:51.450 --> 15:52.750
He wouldn't know.

15:52.820 --> 15:58.120
By the time he left Guardian and arrived here, Bison had already dismantled.

16:05.930 --> 16:07.430
Bison...?

16:08.300 --> 16:11.600
You mean the gang that had supreme power over Hot Clock?

16:11.600 --> 16:16.210
That's right. Riki was the leader of Bison.

16:32.820 --> 16:36.160
Hmm. So he was an incredible guy.

16:36.190 --> 16:38.490
Well, before they dismantled.

16:38.530 --> 16:40.060
He was popular.

16:40.100 --> 16:43.000
No, that's not quite the case.

16:43.030 --> 16:49.070
Yeah. He has a cold appearance, but it's hard to take your eyes off him.

16:57.810 --> 17:01.420
But, how does he muster the courage to come back now?

17:01.450 --> 17:04.490
Yeah, it's unsightly.

17:04.520 --> 17:07.360
He's a disgrace to Guy's group, too.

17:07.390 --> 17:12.690
In the end, Bison and Riki are just losers.

17:36.150 --> 17:39.560
So it's been three months since you've returned?

17:39.590 --> 17:42.490
Shut up and just get it over with.

17:42.520 --> 17:43.930
Yes, yes.

17:49.630 --> 17:52.300
It wasn't three months.

17:52.330 --> 17:54.700
It's been three years since then...

18:01.440 --> 18:03.910
Yo, how you doing?

18:09.690 --> 18:11.290
You all right?

18:13.170 --> 18:15.690
Here's a little present.

18:17.760 --> 18:19.660
What's with this?

18:25.130 --> 18:27.600
You seem to be in high spirits.

18:28.140 --> 18:30.470
Did something good happen?

18:30.470 --> 18:31.870
Kind of.

18:33.240 --> 18:38.050
Anyway, can't believe you managed to get a bottle of Roger Lina.

18:40.880 --> 18:43.920
What, are you mocking me?

18:43.950 --> 18:45.120
No.

18:45.150 --> 18:51.430
I just wanted to thank you. I rarely get branded goods.

18:51.460 --> 18:55.130
I'm not thinking that you stole it from somewhere or anything.

18:59.370 --> 19:05.640
Hey, Riki. You're not mixed up in any trouble, are you?

19:06.540 --> 19:09.080
What's this?

19:09.110 --> 19:11.280
Hey, don't glare at me.

19:11.310 --> 19:14.180
Don't avoid my question.

19:17.920 --> 19:24.760
Hey Guy. Opportunities don't come often, do they?

19:25.360 --> 19:31.500
Especially for people like us, there's hardly ever a chance to see the greater world.

19:31.900 --> 19:38.970
I'm tired of sneaking around and living like this.

19:39.390 --> 19:44.650
If I stay here, I feel like I'll rot to the core of my body.

19:45.880 --> 19:49.850
I'm getting the hell out of here.

20:15.480 --> 20:17.410
Oh yeah, did you know?

20:17.410 --> 20:21.150
There's gonna be a market at Mistral Park!

20:21.220 --> 20:24.620
Market? Is that a pet auction?

20:24.650 --> 20:28.720
Yup! Apparently the pets of the Academy will be there too this time.

20:28.760 --> 20:33.000
Academy pets, huh. They're the ones with the pure blood.

20:40.400 --> 20:42.600
That's got nothing to do with us.

20:42.770 --> 20:47.580
I want to compare myself to the Academy pets.

20:47.610 --> 20:52.180
We'd fit in well enough if only we put enough time and money into it.

20:52.210 --> 20:53.850
Right, Riki?

20:59.520 --> 21:00.920
What's up, Kirie?

21:00.920 --> 21:03.960
Do you want a collar with your name on it?

21:04.530 --> 21:09.530
Of course! If my owner would let me drink premium Dublin grade booze,

21:09.560 --> 21:12.130
I'd even lick the soles of his feet.

21:17.770 --> 21:20.740
What the hell are you blabbering about?

21:20.740 --> 21:25.910
There's no way anyone would want to take scum of the Slum as a pet.

21:34.260 --> 21:38.390
Come on, stop talking and drink.

21:38.760 --> 21:41.400
Luke! Stop it, you!

21:43.070 --> 21:44.430
What's wrong, Riki?

21:44.470 --> 21:46.700
What's with that brat?

21:48.900 --> 21:51.210
Our mascot?

21:51.240 --> 21:54.540
Or more precisely, the self-nominated mascot?

21:54.580 --> 21:58.310
Well, I actually have no idea what he's thinking.

21:58.560 --> 22:01.350
He's not a loser groupie, is he?

22:02.120 --> 22:04.220
He's not doing any harm right now.

22:05.590 --> 22:08.460
Even if he doesn't cause you guys trouble,

22:08.490 --> 22:12.460
everything about him puts me on edge.

22:13.130 --> 22:16.930
I feel strangely angry whenever he's around.

22:17.330 --> 22:18.770
Why?

22:30.880 --> 22:32.480
I feel like getting drunk.

22:33.320 --> 22:34.480
Riki...?

22:45.830 --> 22:48.630
Three years of separation.

22:49.400 --> 22:53.640
But you won't tell me anything, Riki.
